    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d789">

                <pb facs="0893" n="1727" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/604</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-15T12:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 15, 1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/>
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 16, 12.23
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1952. Council of Ministers decided last night to take temporary possession of
                    seven German vessels refugeed in Spanish ports, as follows: <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eriphia, Euphemia, Oldenburg, Klio, Mathilde</hi>, [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Siegfried</hi>], <hi rendition="#italic">Rudolf</hi>.
                    Total tonnage approximately 21,000. This decision was arrived at after prolonged
                    and friendly negotiations with Germany, and in said decision Germany has
                    apparently acquiesced.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
